Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: rg35xx-sp: run RAM rail at 1.2V for LPDDR3

The shared RG35XX device tree pins vdd-dram at 1.1V for LPDDR4. Without this
override, Linux would undervolt the LPDDR3 RAM on this unit during boot.
ROCKNIX applies the same voltage through its H700 ddr3 overlay.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-sp.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-sp.dts
@@ -32,3 +32,9 @@
 		reg = <0x51>;
 	};
 };
+
+/* This unit has LPDDR3 RAM, which runs at 1.2V rather than the LPDDR4 1.1V. */
+&reg_dcdc3 {
+	regulator-min-microvolt = <1200000>;
+	regulator-max-microvolt = <1200000>;
+};
